1
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:09,230
♪La la la la la la, la la la la la la♪

2
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:12,740
♪La la la la la la la la la♪

3
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:16,329
♪No matter what day it is,
I'll spend it with you♪

4
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:19,100
♪We're more sure
of each other than ever♪

5
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,060
=Watching Heart Signal with You=

6
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,620
(Before filming the watch-along)

7
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,320
I just remembered the last watch-along.

8
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,360
You guys sat so far apart.

9
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:26,320
Yeah.

10
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:27,640
We were sitting like you guys too.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,280
One plate of fruit.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,320
If these sisters really went for it...

13
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,520
You'd need four full plates.

14
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,160
No.

15
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,440
You could cover this whole table
in fruit, and they'd still...

16
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,280
Four plates,
and they'd only leave half a plate.

17
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:41,200
That's why we love going to bathhouses.

18
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,600
No, those bathhouse fruit buffets

19
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,160
are basically made for these two.

20
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,400
You can get drinks too.

21
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,280
After the next episode airs,
let's go to one.

22
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:49,760
Sure.

23
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:52,120
Hewen's here.

24
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,240
Hey,

25
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,240
I saw that post about you...

26
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,680
Getting spotted.

27
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,200
Hewen in person.

28
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,200
Tall and handsome.

29
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:01,200
Lately I keep

30
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:01,880
running into people.

31
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:02,920
But actually...

32
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,040
It's totally on purpose.

33
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:05,880
It really isn't.

34
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:08,560
That's too much, Yihang.

35
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,920
Get him. Smack him twice for me, Bohan.

36
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,920
Si, want some fruit?

37
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:14,440
Sure.

38
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,000
This is winter melon.

39
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:17,680
Cantaloupe.

40
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:23,240
Come on, Yihang. Play me tomorrow.

41
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:24,320
Sure, no problem.

42
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,640
A badminton match?

43
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:27,960
There's one today and tomorrow.

44
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:28,960
I'll go easy on you.

45
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:29,880
Since you're the pro.

46
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:31,920
Cheers.

47
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:32,280
Come on.

48
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,120
Let's do it.

49
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,080
Welcome, everyone.

50
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:39,080
Welcome.

51
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,440
Let's introduce ourselves.

52
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,240
Let's do introductions.

53
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:42,800
Hi, everyone.

54
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,960
I'm Wu Xingying

55
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:44,920
(Wu Xingying)
from

56
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:45,440
Heart Signal 9.

57
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:45,960
Hi, everyone.

58
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,520
(Wu Siying)
I'm Wu Siying

59
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,280
from Heart Signal 9.

60
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:48,760
Hi, everyone.

61
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,320
I'm Cui Yihang

62
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,200
(Cui Yihang)
from Heart Signal 9.

63
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:51,840
Hi, everyone.

64
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,960
(Sun Bohan)
I'm Bohan

65
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:53,960
from Heart Signal 9.

66
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:54,480
Hi, everyone.

67
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:55,760
(Chen Hewen)
I'm Chen Hewen

68
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,080
from Heart Signal 9.

69
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:57,920
Welcome, Little Baoyu.

70
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,680
Okay.

71
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:00,680
Welcome.

72
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,720
This is my first time watching

73
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,840
with the family of four

74
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,400
together.

75
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,200
Now we're a family of five.

76
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,400
So what do we say?

77
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,199
What do we say
when we meet a real couple?

78
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,400
Nine-Nine.

79
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:13,440
And you call yourself the king of jokes.

80
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,240
What joke?

81
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,160
You should be sitting in the middle.

82
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:16,520
Yeah.

83
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,720
I really should've sat in the middle.

84
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,240
I could tease this side,

85
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,000
then tease that side.

86
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Family of five.

87
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,280
My outfit color

88
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:21,760
really clashes with yours.

89
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,520
You guys are all

90
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,040
pink and white, white and pink.

91
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,400
Did you plan this?

92
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,040
Coincidence.

93
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,360
Total coincidence.

94
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,000
What are you guys called?

95
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,080
What's your slogan?

96
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:30,880
Do you have a code?

97
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,720
I don't know what a code is.

98
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,320
Oh, I get it.

99
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,200
You have a string of numbers,

100
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,720
and that's your couple name.

101
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:39,280
He was just setting that up

102
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,200
so we'd bring it up.

103
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,520
Ask it again.

104
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,000
Do you guys have a code?

105
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:45,680
If I remember right,

106
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,320
yours is 4199.

107
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:48,920
Of course you...

108
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,440
Nice.

109
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,320
That's sweet.

110
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,040
You really keep up with us.

111
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:56,360
How've you guys been lately?

112
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,760
Everyone, how's life?

113
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,240
Pretty good.

114
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,000
You two are really settled now.

115
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,120
You can tell just by looking.

116
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:03,960
Look at you.

117
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,840
I'm doing amazing.

118
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,480
No.

119
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,880
No, I'm kidding.

120
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,200
Should we start watching?

121
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:11,760
Let's start.

122
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,440
Okay.

123
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,280
Put this on.

124
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,160
Okay, I'm ready.

125
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,560
Let's see how sweet you guys get today.

126
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:21,660
(Beijing)

127
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,680
You probably went to the hospital first.

128
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:32,720
So handsome.

129
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:37,910
Welcome Back.

130
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:38,960
Welcome Back.

131
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:39,800
Welcome back.

132
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,160
How fitting. Welcome Back.

133
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:41,680
Welcome Back.

134
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,960
It was the second time too.

135
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:43,400
Yeah.

136
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,360
She couldn't use her phone then,
so I got her

137
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:45,880
A book to read.

138
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:46,680
A book.

139
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,130
His teeth arrived before he did.

140
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,760
Teeth first.

141
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:55,140
Hi, Xing.

142
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:57,000
(Smiles)
Hi, Xing.

143
00:03:57,070 --> 00:03:58,130
(So happy)
Look at that smile.

144
00:03:58,290 --> 00:03:58,840
You're here.

145
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,760
Always holding that microphone.

146
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:00,420
I was reading.

147
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,200
The microphone is back.

148
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,500
This is the book you brought last time.

149
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:06,280
You...

150
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,800
(Sits)
I looked so awkward back then.

151
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:08,480
Not at all.

152
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,960
That was only your second time meeting.

153
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,160
Did you feel a little more comfortable?

154
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,480
I was still a little shy.

155
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,440
Look, my ears

156
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,320
were already red.

157
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,360
And my neck

158
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,600
couldn't turn.

159
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,120
I told him back then I could only...

160
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,279
He could only sit on one side of me.

161
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,600
You couldn't move your head,
just your eyes.

162
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:23,160
Yeah.

163
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,080
Aren't both sisters like that?

164
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:24,640
Head still, eyes moving.

165
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,160
Yeah, like this.

166
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:28,760
No.

167
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:31,660
You can already have liquids.

168
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:32,320
That's great.

169
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:34,230
You recovered pretty fast.

170
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:37,590
Want some water?

171
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:38,570
I'll get you some.

172
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,800
Look at my ears.

173
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,320
You two weren't close yet?

174
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:43,150
This adjusts the temperature.

175
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:43,920
We were still a little awkward.

176
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,660
How much of the book did you read?

177
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:45,930
A little.

178
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,320
Mostly, I just

179
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:48,580
didn't want you to get bored here.

180
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,660
So I thought I'd find you a book.

181
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:51,860
It's a story about Northeast China.

182
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:52,880
Yeah, a story from Northeast China.

183
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:53,760
Northeast China.

184
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,880
I was worried she wouldn't get into it.

185
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,680
I did read it.

186
00:04:59,110 --> 00:04:59,850
No, I need some self-control.

187
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,960
I barely ate today.

188
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:02,200
Maybe don't.

189
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:02,940
Yeah.

190
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:03,210
No.

191
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:04,700
I mean, eat whatever you want...

192
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:07,860
while you still can.

193
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,360
Xing kept telling us

194
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,760
everyone in the house
should eat properly.

195
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:11,280
Yeah, eat properly.

196
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:11,720
Yeah.

197
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,160
She brought us bread back then

198
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,520
so everyone would eat breakfast.

199
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:18,240
What do you want to eat
once you're better?

200
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:20,610
Everything, right?

201
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,920
First up has to be an iron-pot stew.

202
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:23,400
Don't you think?

203
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:24,880
Honestly, I love it.

204
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:25,200
I really love it.

205
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:25,680
Yeah.

206
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,160
I think iron-pot stew
is really good too.

207
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,720
You just enjoy
your donkey-meat sandwich.

208
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,470
Is it hot outside today?

209
00:05:32,470 --> 00:05:33,680
Yeah, pretty hot today.

210
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,640
Why am I making that face?

211
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,440
You were acting cute.

212
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:42,480
Why were you acting cute?

213
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,680
I barely recognize you, Bohan.

214
00:05:45,110 --> 00:05:45,680
Last night,

215
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,000
I had a dream.

216
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,500
I dreamed you said something really...

217
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,480
Seeing her all day wasn't enough?

218
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,660
You had to see her in your dreams too?

219
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:54,780
You said something really...

220
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:55,400
Even his dreams are busy.

221
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,590
Really coldhearted.

222
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,320
(Something really coldhearted)
What?

223
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,390
What?

224
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,790
What did I say?

225
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,600
How did you put it again?

226
00:06:03,410 --> 00:06:03,960
You said,

227
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,890
"I don't feel anything for you anymore."

228
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,320
(Going into detail)
I don't feel anything for you anymore.

229
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:09,600
Look at that smile.

230
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,680
What are you laughing at?

231
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,920
I remember how you smiled at me then.

232
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:14,440
You thought it was funny.

233
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:14,920
I really did dream that.

234
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,080
I thought it was hilarious.

235
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,520
(Going into detail)
We did a bunch of things in the dream.

236
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,890
Then in the car, you suddenly said it.

237
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:22,240
(Holding back laughter)
You just said that out of nowhere.

238
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,290
When I woke up, I thought,

239
00:06:23,290 --> 00:06:23,980
no way.

240
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:25,730
I have to clear this up with you today.

241
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:26,970
Were you trying to tell me something

242
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:27,510
in my dream?

243
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,200
You came here to pick a fight.

244
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,080
For a few days,

245
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,760
I dreamed about her every night.

246
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,360
And in the dreams, she'd usually say

247
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,480
something pretty upsetting.

248
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,760
Something hurtful.

249
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:36,640
Dreams mean the opposite.

250
00:06:38,650 --> 00:06:40,790
I brought our letters too.

251
00:06:41,670 --> 00:06:42,580
Our letters?

252
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:47,520
I don't even need to look now.

253
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,560
I already know which one's which.

254
00:06:48,570 --> 00:06:49,440
(This one's from day one)
How can you tell?

255
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,960
You can feel the creases in the letters?

256
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,080
I think each day's letter...

257
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:53,680
Had a little mark.

258
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,520
A little mark.

259
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,440
And with those marks,

260
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,960
plus reading them over and over,

261
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,160
I just memorized them.

262
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,680
Every day, Xing had Si pass on messages.

263
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,360
Did Si

264
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,640
pass them on accurately?

265
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:06,800
Not really.

266
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,400
She even forgot once.

267
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,600
Just that one time.

268
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,760
Because he was by the door that day.

269
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:12,440
You really forgot?

270
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,480
You distracted me.

271
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,800
He messed with my head.

272
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,640
Messed with my head.

273
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,520
Every time Si

274
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:23,280
passed on a message,
it'd just be one sentence.

275
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,440
But the meaning was probably the same.

276
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,560
Si told me privately

277
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,360
that whenever Xing gave her a message,

278
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,600
she'd make Si repeat it back.

279
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:30,560
I'd make her repeat it several times.

280
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,800
And she still couldn't remember.

281
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,600
Blame me.

282
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,920
I was too distracting for Si.

283
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,000
You threw her off.

284
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,320
Mostly because she'd walk
into the house and see me.

285
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,640
Maybe she'd get a little flustered.

286
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,120
Okay.

287
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:41,880
Sorry.

288
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,360
